Change: Require `--include` for `restore --target / --delete`

A snapshot also contains the parent directories of the backed up paths. When
running `restore --target / --delete`, restic therefore deleted unrelated files
next to the backed up paths, for example `/mnt/test/other-content` for a
snapshot of `/mnt/test/data`. The safeguard against this could be bypassed by
specifying only an `--exclude` option.

`restore --target / --delete` now requires an `--include` option, which limits
the files that may be deleted. Alternatively, restore a subfolder using the
`snapshotID:subfolder` syntax to the matching target directory.

The `restore` command now also allows combining `--include` and `--exclude`
options. Exclude patterns then remove files from the set of files selected by
the include patterns.

